title: 'A run''s times are logged in three places: a suite''s by phase, a server''s by span, a session''s by tool call.'
pid: d21ac1dd-eca7-4549-85af-9e120fd72a19
body: |2-
  - A suite: 'tests/results/ALL.org' gives each phase's and each
    integration directory's seconds. 'bash/all-tests.sh' deletes it
    when it starts, so copy it to keep it.
  - A server: with 'timing_log = true', 'server.jsonl' in the run folder
    has a 'close' event for every span, with 'time.busy': select with
    jq the records whose '.fields.message' is "close", and print
    '.span.name' and '.fields["time.busy"]'. Startup is the 'initialize_dbs' close and "Server ready"
    in 'server-to-user.log'.
  - A session: only Claude Code's transcripts. A tool call lasts from the
    assistant record holding its 'tool_use' to the user record holding
    its 'tool_result'. The spending account holds tokens and a session's
    start and end, not its tool calls.
    'tools/introspect/machine-measures/where_sessions_wait.py' sums the
    gaps by what ended them (the model, a test, a build, ...) for each
    kind of row in the account.
  Read that way, 2026-11-10 to 15: the model's own time was 77% of all
  working time, tests 8%, builds 2%; in build missions the model 65%,
  tests 23%.
